    feat: add lead capture to all six interactive tools
    
    - New server route: app/api/tools/capture/route.ts
      Mirrors the hardening from the contact form: origin check, content-type
      validation, IP extraction, rate limiting (5/hr via Upstash Redis,
      degrades gracefully), honeypot field, required-field and type validation.
      Forwards validated data to HUB_API_URL/api/public/leads with
      HUB_PUBLIC_API_KEY server-side only (via hubFetch). Never exposes the
      key to the browser.
    
    - New component: components/ToolLeadCapture.tsx
      Client component with name, email, optional company, hidden honeypot,
      and submit button. Shows confirmation on success, error state on
      failure, loading state during submission. Result is never gated behind
      the form — capture sits below the result.
    
    - Wired into all six tools:
      - ops-health-score: summary = score/25 + health label
      - ai-readiness-check: summary = score/10 + result label
      - automation-roi-calculator: summary = ROI% + break-even
      - downtime-cost-calculator: summary = hourly cost + annual total
      - rto-calculator: summary = annual saving + 3-year saving
      - should-i-replace-erp: summary = score + recommendation label
    
    - Added toolCaptureRatelimit to lib/rate-limit.ts
    - Added HUB_PUBLIC_API_KEY to .env.example
    
    TypeScript compiles clean (npx tsc --noEmit). No new dependencies.

